{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":279745,"name":"Brett Cannon","username":"brettcannon","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/brettcannon/{size}/34895_2.png","created_at":"2025-12-08T19:31:22.481Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0816/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/7/8/7808f673c94c5abc6cdd738548e39c7ae50dc418.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"979F6B\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0816/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ePython Enhancement Proposals (PEPs)\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cimg width=\"200\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/8/3/8354042ac932196b5fde1d1048a76b567decdcdc.png\" class=\"thumbnail onebox-avatar\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"9EAC81\"\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0816/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ePEP 816 – WASI Support | peps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eThis PEP outlines the expected support for WASI by CPython. It contains enough details to know what WASI and WASI SDK version is expected to be supported for any release of CPython while official WASI support is specified in PEP 11.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe executive summary is:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLock down WASI and WASI SDK version support at b1 for the life of a Python version and write it down in PEP 11\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChanges to the WASI SDK version after b1 requires writing down why\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChanges to the WASI version require SC approval\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdating the target triple for \u003ccode\u003emain\u003c/code\u003e in PEP 11 doesn’t require anything special.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’ve cleared this with the appropriate folks at the Bytecode Alliance and our current and future RMs are aware of it.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2025-12-08T19:45:29.658Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":120,"reads":191,"readers_count":190,"score":843.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":105237,"topic_slug":"pep-816-wasi-support","display_username":"Brett Cannon","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"packaging-council","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/0/5/05b580b0d5d0ba0258ddcb3685ca7006fcd0f01b.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":48,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0816/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 816 – WASI Support | peps.python.org","clicks":99},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-specifying-wasi-support/105238","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"PEP specifying WASI support","clicks":4}],"read":true,"user_title":"Packaging Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":14}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":36,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-816-wasi-support/105237/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":14}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":14,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":282231,"name":"Brett Cannon","username":"brettcannon","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/brettcannon/{size}/34895_2.png","created_at":"2026-01-09T20:05:36.120Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for the hearts! I’ve \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/steering-council/issues/329\"\u003esent this to the SC\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-01-09T20:05:36.120Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":116,"readers_count":115,"score":43.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":105237,"topic_slug":"pep-816-wasi-support","display_username":"Brett Cannon","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"packaging-council","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/0/5/05b580b0d5d0ba0258ddcb3685ca7006fcd0f01b.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":48,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/python/steering-council/issues/329","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 816 -- WASI Support · Issue #329 · python/steering-council · GitHub","clicks":16}],"read":true,"user_title":"Packaging Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":36,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-816-wasi-support/105237/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":286504,"name":"Donghee Na","username":"corona10","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/corona10/{size}/9943_2.png","created_at":"2026-02-27T02:23:45.081Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi Brett,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn behalf of the Steering Council, I’m pleased to inform you that \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0816/\"\u003ePEP 816\u003c/a\u003e has been approved. Congratulations!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, we would like the PEP to clarify who bears the responsibility of keeping \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0011/\"\u003ePEP 11\u003c/a\u003e up to date, and when this is done (when the build scripts are updated, or on release of beta 1, or at some other point of time).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThank you for your patience and for your work on this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWarm regards,\u003cbr\u003e\nDonghee\u003cbr\u003e\n(on behalf of the Python Steering Council)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-02-27T02:23:45.081Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":77,"reads":105,"readers_count":104,"score":501.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":105237,"topic_slug":"pep-816-wasi-support","display_username":"Donghee Na","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"steering-council","flair_url":"fab-python","flair_bg_color":"FFE873","flair_color":"4B8BBE","flair_group_id":45,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0816/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 816 – WASI Support | peps.python.org","clicks":18},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0011/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 11 – CPython platform support | peps.python.org","clicks":10},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/2026-02-26-python-steering-council-meeting-summary/106311","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"2026-02-26 Python Steering Council Meeting Summary","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"Steering